Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:34:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gateway: a raw control byte in a request's strings is
 escaped, and the turn goes on
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A Codex turn that read a binary file whole carried a raw control byte
(0x00-0x1F) inside one of its strings, and the gateway refused the
whole turn: 6.8 MB and 7.5 MB bodies of one thread, refused on
`invalid character '\x00' in string literal` - magpie's own 400, no
usage row, nothing routed (AnxForever, #5668). A raw control byte in a
string is what JSON forbids, and \u00XX is the same character in the
only spelling the grammar takes. A control byte outside a string is a
broken structure escaping cannot mend, and that refusal stays.

decodeRequest is the one JSON gate a client request passes before
fields are rewritten or it is routed: handle, countTokens, gemini and
the Codex backend's own /responses all read through it, and now
Ollama's /api/chat and /api/generate do too, whose own json.Unmarshal
refused the same way - what they route is the rebuild of what they
decoded, so the mended parse is what goes out. A body that parses is
walked never, rewritten never, logged never: the fallback costs one
failed parse, nothing more. A body that failed is walked once, its
strings' raw control bytes escaped, the copy parsed again, and what
parses is the body routed, with one line said of it - how many, the
offset of the first, an excerpt. A body the copy does not mend is
refused with the first parse's error, not the repair's.

The translators read the body decodeRequest hands them, so a turn that
needed no escape is translated byte for byte as before, and one that
did goes out valid whatever protocol it is spoken in.

Run: go test -tags nogui -run 'RawControlByte|EscapeRawControlBytes|
DecodeRequest|ParsedRequest|EscapeFallback|OllamaChatRawControl'
./internal/gateway ok, 9 named tests, Gemini/Codex/Count/Ollama
domains green. The codex one is red with the escape branch dead again
(the NUL rides to the backend as a 400), green restored. gofmt -l
clean.
Not tried: the reporter's Codex CLI 0.167.0 on Windows against a real
6.8 MB turn; the shape is reproduced on a fake upstream instead.

